{%- comment -%}
  GummyChums quality/certifications — real cert data, no invented claims.

  Two layouts, because the homepage and the story page want different things
  from the same facts:

  "badges"  a single scannable row of short labels and a link to the detail.
            Six paragraph cards on the homepage ran 1,572px on a phone and asked
            for a page of reading before anyone had reached the products.
  "full"    the six cards with licence numbers and certificate references, for
            /pages/story where somebody has chosen to go deeper.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign s = section.settings -%}
{%- comment -%}
  No licence or certificate NUMBERS on the site. Mehal: "remove certificates
  and fssai, no one puts it on website" — and he is right about the convention;
  Indian D2C brands show the badge, not the paperwork.

  What stays, deliberately: the "FSSAI licensed" badge (a claim, not an
  identifier), the manufacturer's name and address in the footer, and the
  not-evaluated-by-FSSAI disclaimer. Those are different things from a licence
  number and should not be swept out with it.
{%- endcomment -%}
<style>
  .gcq{background:var(--role-quiet-bg);padding:clamp(var(--sp-8),7vw,var(--sp-9)) var(--gutter)}
  /* the rail is a thin ruled band, not a section with a headline */
  .gcq--strip{padding-block:clamp(var(--sp-6),4vw,var(--sp-7))}
  .gcq--strip .gcq-in{border-top:1px solid var(--role-line);border-bottom:1px solid var(--role-line);
    padding-block:clamp(var(--sp-5),3vw,var(--sp-6))}
  .gcq--strip .gcq-badges{margin-top:0}
  .gcq-in{max-width:var(--container);margin-inline:auto}
  .gcq-kick{font-weight:var(--fw-black);letter-spacing:var(--ls-wide);text-transform:uppercase;font-size:var(--fs-xs);color:var(--c-accent);margin:0}
  /* `margin: … auto …` was still centring this after the section went
     left-aligned, so the heading floated while the kicker, the actives line and
     the link all sat at the left edge. Scale raised to match the other
     editorial sections. */
  .gcq-title{font-size:var(--fs-3xl);font-weight:var(--fw-black);
    letter-spacing:var(--ls-tight);line-height:.99;color:var(--role-page-ink);
    margin:var(--sp-4) 0 0;max-width:20ch}
  .gcq-sub{font-size:var(--fs-base);font-weight:var(--fw-body);color:var(--c-ink-2);margin:var(--sp-4) 0 0;max-width:46ch;line-height:var(--lh-body)}

  /* ---- badges ---- */
  /* max-width:840px forced a wrap after four, leaving "No added sugar" alone on
     a second row — an orphan that read as an afterthought. The five fit on one
     line inside the container. */
  .gcq-badges{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;justify-content:flex-start;gap:var(--sp-3);
    margin:var(--sp-6) 0 0}
  .gcq-actives{margin:var(--sp-4) 0 0;font-size:var(--fs-sm);color:var(--role-ink-muted)}
  /* These were white pills on a cream ground — a trust row that read as more
     cream. They cycle the three product tones so the rail carries the brand's
     colour without a band behind it. The ink stays dark on every one of them:
     cream on mango is 2.6:1 and fails, which is why the tint is light and the
     text is not. */
  /* .gc-mark reserves its own 20px via padding-left and draws the pixel at
     left:0. This rule's `padding` shorthand overwrote that reservation, so the
     pixel rendered hard against the pill's border. The space is reserved here
     instead, and the mark is pushed in to sit level with the text. */
  .gcq-badge{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:var(--sp-2);
    background:var(--c-surface);border:2px solid var(--role-page-ink);
    border-radius:var(--r-full);padding:var(--sp-2) var(--sp-5);
    font-size:var(--fs-sm);font-weight:var(--fw-black);color:var(--role-page-ink);
    box-shadow:3px 3px 0 var(--role-page-ink)}
  .gcq-badge.gc-mark{padding-left:calc(var(--sp-5) + 20px)}
  .gcq-badge.gc-mark::before{left:var(--sp-5)}
  .gcq-badge:nth-child(3n+1){background:color-mix(in srgb, var(--c-mango) 34%, var(--c-surface))}
  .gcq-badge:nth-child(3n+2){background:color-mix(in srgb, var(--c-orange) 30%, var(--c-surface))}
  .gcq-badge:nth-child(3n+3){background:color-mix(in srgb, var(--c-cherry) 26%, var(--c-surface))}

  /* ---- full cards ---- */
  /* A LEDGER, NOT A CARD GRID.
     This was repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr)) under a centred heading — six identical
     boxes, the same shape as every other section. The copy already promises
     "backed by paperwork, not vibes", so the section now looks like paperwork:
     ruled rows, the claim on the left, the detail beside it, the certificate
     number in the right-hand column where a reference belongs. Nothing here is
     decorated, which is the point. */
  .gcq-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:0;text-align:left;
    border-top:2px solid var(--role-page-ink);margin-top:var(--sp-6)}
  .gcq-card{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,20ch) minmax(0,1fr) minmax(0,24ch);
    gap:var(--sp-5);align-items:start;padding:var(--sp-5) 0;
    border-bottom:1px solid var(--role-line);background:none;box-shadow:none;border-radius:0}
  .gcq-card:hover{background:var(--c-surface)}
  .gcq-card b{display:block;font-size:var(--fs-base);font-weight:var(--fw-black);color:var(--c-ink);margin:0}
  .gcq-card p{font-size:var(--fs-sm);font-weight:var(--fw-body);color:var(--c-ink-2);line-height:var(--lh-body);margin:0}
  .gcq-card span.gcq-ref{display:block;font-size:var(--fs-xs);font-weight:var(--fw-bold);
    color:var(--c-ink-3);margin:0;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;text-align:right}
  @media(max-width:899px){
    .gcq-card{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:var(--sp-2)}
    .gcq-card span.gcq-ref{text-align:left}
  }

  .gcq-note{font-size:var(--fs-xs);font-weight:var(--fw-body);color:var(--c-ink-3);margin:var(--sp-8) auto 0;max-width:52ch;line-height:var(--lh-body)}


  @media (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.gcq-card{transition:none}}
</style>

<section class="gcq{% if s.layout == 'badges' %} gcq--strip{% endif %}">
  <div class="gcq-in">
    {%- if s.layout == 'badges' -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        A RAIL, NOT A SECTION.
        This carried a kicker, a 56px heading, a lede, a certificate card and a
        "See the certificates" button — a full content section for something
        nobody scrolls a homepage to read. Three of its five badges already
        scroll past in the announcement marquee at the top of the same page.
        The licence number lives in the footer, where it is legally required
        and where people actually look for it. What is left is the rail.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="gcq-badges gc-rise">
        <span class="gcq-badge gc-mark">FSSAI licensed</span>
        <span class="gcq-badge gc-mark">Every batch lab-tested</span>
        <span class="gcq-badge gc-mark">100% vegetarian</span>
        <span class="gcq-badge gc-mark">Made in India</span>
        <span class="gcq-badge gc-mark">No added sugar</span>
      </div>
      <p class="gcq-actives">Bacopa · Melatonin · Lutein</p>

    {%- else -%}
      <p class="gcq-kick">{{ s.kicker }}</p>
      <h2 class="gcq-title">{{ s.title }}</h2>
      <p class="gcq-sub">{{ s.sub }}</p>
      <div class="gcq-grid">
        <div class="gcq-card">
                    <b class="gc-mark">FSSAI licensed manufacturing</b>
          <p>Made in a facility holding a Central FSSAI license under the Food Safety &amp; Standards Act, 2006.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="gcq-card">
                    <b class="gc-mark">GMP certified</b>
          <p>Independently audited and certified to Good Manufacturing Practice by Eurofins Assurance India.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="gcq-card">
                    <b class="gc-mark">FSSC 22000 certified</b>
          <p>Our manufacturer's food safety management system is certified to FSSC 22000 (ISO 22000:2018 based).</p>
        </div>
        <div class="gcq-card">
                    <b class="gc-mark">Every batch, lab-tested</b>
          <p>Each batch is checked for microbial load, yeast &amp; mould and heavy metals before it ships — every result on file.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="gcq-card">
                    <b class="gc-mark">100% vegetarian</b>
          <p>Pectin-based gummies — no gelatin, no animal-derived ingredients, ever.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="gcq-card">
                    <b class="gc-mark">Proudly made in India</b>
          <p>Formulated and manufactured in Greater Noida, Uttar Pradesh — no importing, no middlemen.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="gcq-card">
                    <b class="gc-mark">No added sugar</b>
          <p>Sweetened without added sugar — the actives are Bacopa, Melatonin and Lutein, one to a gummy.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="gcq-note">{{ s.disclaimer }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</section>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "GummyChums Quality",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "select", "id": "layout", "label": "Layout",
      "info": "Badges for the homepage — a scannable row plus a link. Full cards for the story page, where people have chosen to read.",
      "options": [
        { "value": "badges", "label": "Badge row (short)" },
        { "value": "full", "label": "Full cards (detailed)" }
      ], "default": "full" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "kicker", "label": "Kicker", "default": "✦ The boring but important bit" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "title", "label": "Title", "default": "Real labs. Real certificates. Real gummies." },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "sub", "label": "Full layout — subtitle",
      "default": "We're not just cute — every claim on this page is backed by paperwork, not vibes." },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "disclaimer", "label": "Full layout — disclaimer",
      "default": "Nutraceutical products. These statements have not been evaluated by the FSSAI. Not intended to diagnose, treat, cure, or prevent any disease. Certificates issued to our manufacturer, Biovencer Healthcare Private Limited." }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "GummyChums Quality" }]
}
{% endschema %}
